From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] DIAG: interconnect: sm6375: disable QoS register writes

Diagnostic-only build (v50). Sets qos.ap_owned = false on every node so the
probe path skips qcom_icc_qos_set() entirely: no QoS registers are written,
only RPM clock/bandwidth votes happen. Used to isolate whether a wrong
qos_port is resetting the SoC at boot (v48/v49 hang with no ramoops).

If the SoC boots with this patch, the hang is caused by a QoS register
write to a wrong port/mode and we can re-enable ports incrementally. If it
still hangs, the fault is in the bus reg/regmap/RPM-clock config instead.

REMOVE once QoS is validated.

